  "runObservations": [
    "The previous 25 successful jobs and 75 stages were partial end-to-end evidence only, not proof of full-weekend completeness.",
    "A clean pre-collection baseline database was unavailable. The isolated copy began with 25 previously successful race tasks and 23 active/pending target race tasks. Forty-eight fresh ManualRefresh receipts covered 48 unique expected races; all 48 target resources were executed successfully in this run, including retries where needed.",
    "The initial 48 fresh ManualRefresh requests were partial-run evidence, not by themselves clean-baseline acceptance. After identifying stale payout placeholders and refresh-route defects, 29 additional scoped refresh requests were submitted. Across 77 requests for 48 resources, the latest attempt for every target race succeeded; task history retains two failed tasks and four canceled tasks superseded by later successful revisions.",
    "Historical target failures: one PermanentFailure/ArgumentException on revision 7 because refresh used English course attributes instead of canonical Japanese; one ValidationFailure/RaceResultWriteFailed on revision 10 after the refresh route supplied an empty sourceHorseId. Revision 12 canonicalized course attributes, passed the persisted domainRaceId and null sourceHorseId; all three affected races then persisted successfully. The revision-10 write returned HTTP 500 after payout events were partially committed; explicit refresh now replaces/clears payout snapshots safely.",
    "Process-local CollectionOrchestration:BackgroundSchedulersEnabled=false disabled planning schedulers in the isolated API only; repository default remains enabled. Non-target active tasks were canceled through the supported API in the isolated copy (1,237 canceled rows in the run window); 12 auxiliary Owner tasks and one Horse profile task were acquired before quiescence. Closure verified zero active target/non-target tasks, zero local queue rows and zero undispatched outbox rows.",
    "The collection runner did not report clean completion because its terminal-result polling failed to converge after all target tasks had succeeded. The persisted task/API/domain evidence was checked independently and the isolated services were safely paused/stopped. This is a harness status-polling limitation, not a result-data failure.",
    "One non-target Horse-profile task reached PermanentFailure with HTTP 400 from the Collector-to-local-v2-API subject profile PUT path, not JRA navigation. Static call-path evidence leads from the profile collector to local API contract validation; API tests reproduce HTTP 400 for invalid request identity/name or official-source URL contract violations, while persisted-subject conflicts return 409. The isolated attempt did not retain a safe field-level validation result, so which input triggered this 400 remains unknown and the original payload was not replayed. It was auxiliary to race-detail acquisition and did not affect the 48 results.",
    "The live JRA page E2E regression passed for Nakayama 3R trifecta 3-5-9 at ¥3,870. The final audit found all five modeled payout categories in all 48 races and zero malformed, placeholder or nonpositive modeled payout entries.",
    "The runtime remained local-only: isolated AppData databases and SQLite queue; no AWS or production access."
